  <data name="HelpHowTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>How it works</value></data>
  <data name="HelpHowText" xml:space="preserve"><value>You pick the game, not the port. Each game has one recommended way to play and a single button: Install, Play, Update and play, or Fix it. Lotus Ports handles the download, install and setup, always asking you before changing anything on your PC.</value></data>
  <data name="HelpFilesTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Game files</value></data>
  <data name="HelpFilesText" xml:space="preserve"><value>Ports need the files from your own copy of the original game. Lotus Ports never downloads these files or points to where to get them. It only recognizes files you already have and never changes the original.</value></data>
  <data name="HelpProblemTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>If a game does not open</value></data>
  <data name="HelpProblemText" xml:space="preserve"><value>The game button becomes &quot;Fix it&quot;, with the cause in plain language and a one-click fix. When something cannot be confirmed, Lotus Ports says &quot;not verified&quot; instead of pretending all is well.</value></data>
  <data name="HelpSavesTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Saves</value></data>
  <data name="HelpSavesText" xml:space="preserve"><value>Save protection and backups are handled by Lotus, which already does this for all your games.</value></data>
